        We consider elections where both voters and candidates can be associated with points in a <span class="search-hit mathjax">metric</span> space and voters prefer candidates that are closer to those that are farther away. It is often assumed that the optimal candidate is the one that minimizes the total distance to the voters. Yet, the voting rules often do not have access to the&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('1901.06709v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('1901.06709v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
